From 4d3de79696469e898dc4461b8cb5c64c561bb5e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:03:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diar: external-encoder hook - let a caller redirect encode()
 to a different ggml runtime

docs/one-runtime-merge.md's remaining work item: wire the now-byte-exact CrispASR port of the
encoder+head (previous four commits) into an actual merged runtime, without reimplementing the surrounding
orchestration (mel frontend, streaming window scheduling, arrival-order speaker-cache state, turn decoding),
which is intricate, numerically fragile in places (compress()'s score/threshold logic), and already proven
correct by this project's own history. That orchestration has no ggml dependency in its bookkeeping - only
encode() itself (encoder+head) touches ggml.

Added Session::set_external_encoder() (nemotron_3_diar): an optional std::function matching encode()'s own
signature (packed [speaker_cache|fifo|chunk] embeddings in, per-frame probabilities out). encode()'s first
line delegates to it when set; every other line, and everything upstream of encode() in the class, is
byte-for-byte unchanged when it is not. Exposed via a new C API function,
audiocpp_nemotron3_diar_set_external_encoder (nemotron_3_diar only - the one narrow, documented exception to
this file's own "no family-specific includes" rule), so a host process can plug in a callback that runs the
compute on a different ggml backend - e.g. one already shared with another model in the same process -
without linking against this library's internal types.

Verified: ggml symbol visibility unaffected (llvm-readelf --dyn-syms libaudiocpp.so | grep -c ' (ggml|gguf)_'
still 0); the new symbol is exported (matched by the existing audiocpp_* wildcard in audiocpp.map, no map
changes needed). Behavioural verification (hook unset == today's output, hook set to a CrispASR-side
implementation == correct turns) is the next step, in the composite project.

